					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1629892#post-2469792</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1629892/warm-milk-and-ramen#post-2469792</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 09 Mar 2016 01:54:57 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Kalinin</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2203795</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Neutral voting this one. It's a bit silly to be my sort of thing, and I find the eternal struggle between tech support and the rest of the organization to be pretty well-trod ground at this point.</p> <p>That said, this wasn't bad at all. The Foundation-meets-IT nexus goes predictably, but it's charming enough with the goofy appeasement ritual for the malware. Interestingly enough, the dialogue is a strong point, and that's something that a <em>lot</em> of tales have issues with. This is also something that humanizes the MTF being written about, which is badly needed for Rho-9. This is very much in the spirit of the contest, even if it's not my cup of tea.</p> <p>Solid enough job that this isn't a victim of preference, but I do still have that preference.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
